<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see rain, cool temperatures.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see rain, cool temperatures.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Friday were forecast to see rain across the grainbelt, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see rain throughout the province with highs of 15 to 20 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see rain in the south with highs of 15 to 18 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see rain in the south with highs of 15 to 20 Celsius.</p>
<p>The normal high at this time of year is 25 Celsius.</p>
<p>((--Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
